  "principles": [
    "Permanent canonical records, runtime instances and UE5 asset identities are distinct identity classes.",
    "Aliases may aid lookup or migration but are never accepted as canonical *_id values.",
    "Archived canonical records remain resolvable.",
    "Runtime instance IDs exist only within runtime/session evidence and do not become permanent archive records.",
    "Concrete UE5 asset names are validated by semantic parent lineage where a parent contract exists.",
    "Do not invent canonical IDs for legacy values that do not yet have permanent records."
  ],
